the gate cannot silently rot.\n\nNothing was missing, so no `#[no_mangle]` wrapper had to be added and no\nuntranslated C module had to be back-filled: `driver.c` is the entire library\nand both of its external-linkage functions were already translated.\n\n## Undefined (imported) symbols\n\nThe C `.so` imports `printf@GLIBC_2.2.5` and `strchr@GLIBC_2.2.5` (plus the\nusual weak `_ITM_*` / `__gmon_start__` / `__cxa_finalize`).\n\nThe Rust `.so` imports `printf@GLIBC_2.2.5` (the translation deliberately calls\nlibc `printf` rather than Rust `std::io` so the emitted bytes *and* the stdout\nbuffering behaviour match). It does **not** import `strchr` because `strchr` is\nre-implemented byte-for-byte in `src/driver.rs`; this is an implementation\ndetail that is invisible across the ABI and is covered by the differential\ntests. Its remaining imports (`_Unwind_*`, `malloc`, `memcpy`, `dl_iterate_phdr`,\n…) are libc / libgcc_s runtime support pulled in by Rust `std`.\n\n**0 missing symbols and 0 undefined non-libc symbols in the Rust `.so`.**\nVerified with:\n\n```\nldd -r target/debug/libdriver.so     # no \"undefined symbol\" lines\n```\n"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6976,"cache_read_input_tokens":30285,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":6976,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a2685c3d-ee79-4864-97fb-3b0c1854d5cb","uuid":"49fa586d-5e50-48b5-bddf-c0862ff85720","timestamp":"2026-08-18T06:30:17.016Z"}
